        {
            "parameters": {
                "modelName": "gemini-1.5-flash",
                "messages": {
                    "values": [
                        {
                            "role": "system",
                            "content": "=You are the Oscar Legal Practice Intelligence (LPI) module. Your role is to interpret communications from the Lead Lawyer regarding legal work products waiting for approval.\n\nCONTEXT:\nThe lawyer was sent a draft (via Google Doc) and has replied via chat/email. You must classify their intent.\n\nCLASSIFICATION RULES:\n1. approved: Lawyer intends to finalize, send, or publish. \n   - Keywords: 'ok', 'go', 'looks good', 'send it', 'proceed', 'confirmed'.\n   - Special Rule: If the lawyer implies they edited the doc themselves (e.g., 'I fixed it', 'I have edited the doc'), classify as approved.\n2. revise: Lawyer wants the AI to make changes based on text instructions.\n   - Keywords: 'Change the...', 'Add a clause...', 'Redo it'.\n   - Trigger if specific change instructions are detected or if a file is attached.\n3. rejected: Lawyer wants to discard the work.\n   - Keywords: 'discard', 'delete', 'stop', 'no', 'reject'.\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT:\nReturn ONLY a JSON object:\n{\n  \"approval_decision\": \"approved\" | \"rejected\" | \"revise\",\n  \"revision_feedback\": \"Concise summary of feedback\",\n  \"is_direct_edit\": boolean,\n  \"tone_analysis\": \"Note on lawyer mood\"\n}"
                        },
                        {
                            "role": "user",
                            "content": "=LAWYER'S REPLY: \n\"{{ $json.Body || $json.text || $json.message?.text || $json.data || $json.snippet || '' }}\"\n\nBINARY DATA PRESENT: {{ Object.keys($input.first().binary || {}).length > 0 }}\n\nAnalyze the reply and output the classification JSON."
                        }
                    ]
                },
                "options": {}
            },
            "id": "parse-reply",
            "name": "Parse Lawyer Decision",
            "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatGoogleGemini",
            "typeVersion": 1,
            "position": [
                1520,
                400
            ],
            "credentials": {
                "googlePalmApi": {
                    "id": "gemini-cred-id",
                    "name": "Google Gemini API"
                }
            }
